    "source": "Knock calibration phase A fixture (NOT a shipped engine): C15a 0D cycle-model description of the 2016 Honda Civic 1.5 L L15B7 (turbo, DI). Built by tools/enginedata/epa_turbo_engines.py from cited facts plus the toyota_a25a_fks_gen.json Tier 2/3 rules applied UNCHANGED (as tests/support/fixtures/mazda_skyactiv_g20); nothing is fitted to knock data. TIER TABLE - Tier 1 [C]: compression ratio, cylinder count (SAE 2018-01-0319 Table 8). Tier 1b [D]/[M]: valve events, cam phase and lambda schedules from the EPA NVFEL workbook (2016 Honda 1.5L L15B7 Engine Tier 3 Fuel (EPA NVFEL, 02-04-19)). Tier 2 (frozen descriptor constants, as A25A): Wiebe a 5 / m 2 / 40.3205 deg, ignition delay 3.8632, CA50 MBT 8, Woschni, wall 450 K, head factor 1.1, Cd vs L/D, combustion efficiency, F4 friction. Tier 3 [AS]: bore/stroke where not cited; rod l/r 3.0; pin offset 0; valve heads 0.36/0.30 x bore, 2+2 valves; lift shapes = the A25A's digitised curves stretched to the derived 1 mm events, max lift scaled with the bore (L/D as A25A); 1 mm duration split equally between intake and exhaust; runner quarter-wave at the tuning speed (4000 rpm [AS]) over the intake-open span; runner area = intake valve head area; ports 80/250 mm x head area; plenum 1.2 V_d; lumped (no pipes): exhaust and boost are the turbo configuration's.",
